{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Moses would speak and the Elohim, etc.</b> Perhaps Moses would speak before HaShem words of song and praise, as one receiving the face of the great King, blessed be He, <b>and the Elohim would answer him in a voice</b> — meaning, with the voice mentioned nearby, which is the voice of the shofar, as one who is pleased by his words. Or it may say <b>He would answer him</b> [regarding] what he was speaking to Him, and its saying <b>in a voice</b> means in a great voice, so that the people would hear when He spoke with him, as we wrote above, that through this they would validate his prophecy. And it appears to me that there is an additional level here, for HaShem would respond to the words of Moses, and this is a greater distinction than when HaShem would speak first and Moses would answer Him. And our Sages of blessed memory said (Mekhilta) that it refers to the commandments that they heard from the mouth of Moses, that HaShem would elevate the voice of Moses, etc., and this is the way of derash, like a hammer, etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:30:15.116830342Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}